## Context

ROADMAP's Zotero-train hygiene rider (reserved there as "1020"; filed now
under its race-allocated ID). The completion evidence for the Zotero train
row says "no live `~/.idh` references". Today ~10+ files under scripts/,
rules/, skills/ carry `.idh` strings — a mix of genuinely stale pointers
from the pre-0999 layout and intentional probes (e.g.
tests/test_stale_idh_layout.py detects stale layouts BY DESIGN;
scripts/gen-claude-code-adapter-hooks.py generates hooks that point at
$HOME/.idh — classify whether that is live-by-design or stale).

## Actions

1. Enumerate every `~/.idh` / `.idh` reference in live code (scripts/,
   skills/, rules/, bin/, Makefile — tickets history and projects/ memory
   are records, untouched). Classify each: stale (pre-0999 pointer to a
   location the portable installation no longer guarantees) vs
   intentional (a probe or test that exists to detect stale layouts).
2. Replace stale references with the 0999-portable resolution (the
   harness root resolved at runtime, or the ~/.agents default) — match the
   convention already used by the current install strategy
   (docs/idh-install-strategy.md).
3. Keep intentional probes; record each classification in the log.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Every `.idh` reference in live code is either updated to the
      portable resolution or classified-intentional with a log line
- [x] make check passes (test_stale_idh_layout and friends stay green)
      — all targets green on this branch; the sole failure, tickets/1018:9,
      pre-exists at WAVE_BASE ae22cbe7 (see log)
- [x] No new hard-coded absolute home paths (check-agnostic constraint)
